# E §4.1, E §4.2 step 5 (tally 2.1.6, issue #57, the coordinator's pick P4): one plan move keyed by a list index of 11
# keys, its instances at f3 and f11 (key positions 2 and 10) both refused at src on one day. Key positions compare as
# numbers, so m[f3]'s refusal is the one its reads print. refcore 2.1.5 compared the keys' text, (10,) before (2,), and
# printed m[f11].cash.
=== m.tally
model keys
  tally 2
  on 2025-12-31
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31

source fixture "T's fixture for S's kernel tests (invented values)"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

index flats = [f1, f2, f3, f4, f5, f6, f7, f8, f9, f10, f11]

input amt: money DUK

input d0: date

place src: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

place gone: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..2025-01-05

move m[f in flats]: transfers
  on d0
  when pos(f) == 3 or pos(f) == 11
  leg cash from src to gone amount amt

ask q: bal(src, 2025-01-31)

version facts
  cite fixture
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  amt = 1.00 DUK
  d0 = 2025-01-10
  opening[src] = 500.00 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
  opening[gone] = 0 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
=== expect
q: refused: RUN-LIFESPAN m[f3].cash moves into or out of gone outside its lifespan
  cut 2025-12-31
